     the app sandbox the generator turns on) and uses this file only when the project has none, so the signed app is
     never less sandboxed than the unsigned build of the same tag. A release build is AOT-compiled, so the Dart VM needs
     no JIT entitlement. A notarized app must not carry the debugger entitlement (get-task-allow): release-sign.sh
     removes it from the committed file it signs with. The set the unsigned app embeds is compared with the committed
     set, never signed in (REQ-386, P7 R7). -->
